{
  "requirement": "{cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.criteria.criterion_trait`\n\n`Criterion::execute` receives a context for its\n{term}`requirements.sdk.graph.criteria.source_node` and computes its\ncompleted answer:\n\n```rust,ignore\nuse std::future::Future;\n\npub trait Criterion<D: Domain>: Send + Sized {\n    // ...\n\n    /// Select inputs through cx and compute the completed answer.\n    fn execute(\n        self,\n        cx: &mut ValidationContext<'_, D>,\n    ) -> impl Future<Output = Result<Self::Ok, ValidationError<D::Error>>> + Send;\n\n    // ...\n}\n```\n\nAn `Ok` value is the answer defined by\n{cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.criteria.criterion_trait.answer`.\nAn `Err` value reports a [validation error](validators.md#habeas-req-requirements.sdk.graph.validators.ValidationError).",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "I judged this from the supplied test source only. I did not request any implementation source.\n\n**Obligations derived from `requirements.sdk.graph.criteria.execute`**\n1. `Criterion::execute` runs with a context for the criterion's source node, and inputs are selected through that context.\n2. An `Ok` value is the completed answer (`Criterion::Ok`). That includes a negative answer, and the answer must survive Serde JSON. `Ok` is `Send`.\n3. An `Err` value is a `ValidationError`, which reports a failure rather than an answer.\n\n**Mapping obligations to tests**\n- **Completed answer, including a negative one:**\n  - `agent/tests.rs#fn[deterministic_validation_uses_required_storage_without_an_agent]` runs a deterministic criterion and asserts `result.output().result` is false. It also asserts the rationale, and that the saved evidence has a `Dependency::Node(Node(1), …)` fingerprint, so the context read the source node.\n  - `validation_tests.rs#fn[criterion_decode_errors_are_execution_errors_and_false_is_a_completed_answer]` shows a `false` output is a completed `Ok` answer. It asserts the dependencies, stores the answer, and checks that the stored output is `json!(false)`.\n  - `src/authoring/sdk.rs#mod[tests]/fn[review_graph_persists_and_reuses_a_negative_validation_through_the_sdk]` checks a negative determination end to end. It asserts the `Ok` output, that storing it and loading it back gives the same value (the Serde round trip), and that the reloaded answer is reused without another agent call.\n  - `contracts.rs#fn[validation_and_answer_need_send_without_sync]` verifies and stores an answer through `send(...)` wrappers, so the future and the answer are `Send`. It also checks the stored value reloads with the same output.\n- **Context for the source node and tracked reads:**\n  - `runner_does_not_store_a_missing_agent_error_and_supports_intermediate_calls` shows execution reads the source node, records it as a dependency, and supports intermediate agent calls.\n  - `invalid_typed_submission_is_an_agent_error` asserts the context reads exactly `[1]`, the source node.\n- **`Err` reports a `ValidationError`:**\n  - `runner_does_not_store_a_missing_agent_error_and_supports_intermediate_calls` returns `NoAgentConfigured` and stores nothing.\n  - `resolution_storage_and_callback_errors_are_not_judgments` returns `Graph(\"missing\")` from a callback read and stores nothing.\n  - `invalid_typed_submission_is_an_agent_error` returns `ValidationError::Agent`.\n  - The decode-error test returns `ValidationError::Output` with `is_syntax()` and stores nothing.\n  - `agent_errors_expose_the_agreed_string_payload` checks the `Agent` and `Graph` variants' payload, display text and source.\n\n**Conclusion**\nThe `Ok` path (positive and negative answers, serialization round trip, `Send`) and the `Err` path (several distinct `ValidationError` variants, none persisted) are each exercised with assertions on their outcomes. The source-node context is checked through recorded dependencies and reads. The tests carry `{test}` references to the subject. I found no unaddressed obligation or marking gap.",
